## Phasic workflow
You are to take a phasic approach to this work.

This means:

1. Checking the work repository run log to understand what needs to be done next
2. When recording progress with `work log`, include the current phase you're working on
3. Clearly define a stopping point where your work on this phase is complete and you will wait for the user to review your work or give you new instructions.
    a. Use the `work goal <goal description>` command to set your goal for this phase.
    b. Often run `work goal` without parameters to remember your current goal. (checking it regularly should be part of your todo list, if you maintain one.)
    c. You must file a report using the work command at the completion of the phase. This is vital to transfer findings, progress and other information between phases.
    d. Your todo list must only encompass the completion of the current phase.
    e. Record the yield in run state before stopping: `work state set --stop-reason=yield` — the next session's resume brief depends on it.

YOU MUST STOP AFTER COMPLETION OF A PHASE AND YIELD BACK TO THE USER.
